# MadGraph5 batch script: lt~ lt > qt qt~ NP<=2 NPCP<=2
# in vibegraph_toy_UFO, restricted by restrict_yukawa.dat.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   The two scalar bilinears no Standard-Model vertex writes: the bare
#   `Identity(2,1)` and the bare `Gamma5(2,1)`. Both sit on both Yukawa vertices
#   at different coupling orders, so the s-channel scalar reaches this process as
#   four diagrams -- scalar/scalar, scalar/pseudoscalar, pseudoscalar/scalar and
#   pseudoscalar/pseudoscalar -- beside the vector exchange. The relative phase
#   between a scalar and a pseudoscalar current is what the per-helicity
#   interference of those four measures.
#
# The model path is repo-relative to the vendored UFO; build.sh rewrites it to
# the work-area copy it stages under output/models/. This model is ours, so its
# restrict cards live inside the model directory and are staged with it.
#
# `display interactions` prints the count MadGraph's own interaction splitting
# arrives at (one interaction per coupling-order tuple, import_ufo.add_interaction)
# into the build log, which is where extract_interactions.py reads it from.
#
# The order bound is explicit on every row of this model: an unbounded generate
# runs MadGraph's WEIGHTED search, which would drop the higher-order diagrams the
# interference needs.
import model validation/ufo/vibegraph_toy_UFO-yukawa
display interactions
generate lt~ lt > qt qt~ NP<=2 NPCP<=2
output ll_to_qqx_toy_yukawa -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set use_syst False
done
